["er.request/1",{"definition_version":1,"fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"intent":{"causation":null,"command_id":"cmd-child-dee583d7f7fd66d9bfa866aeca654a992e948cbf703c81c7642d42622cb7d04d","command_type":"aep.entity.create/v1","correlation_id":"protocol-artifact-new","execution_id":null,"expected_revision":null,"payload":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"# Store and executor executable contracts\n\nApproved stages 4–5 of the 2026-09-28 operator plan. Shared typed vocabulary validates in `ess/ess-inputs.yaml`; reuse `entity.recording` coordinates, core lossless public values, and store provider/expectation types.\n\n## Scope\n\nOwn `ess/domains/{store,executor}.yaml`, corresponding components and authored scenario directories, `checks/ess-conformance/src/{store,executor}.rs`, and `docs/ess/{store,executor}-traceability.md`. Shared runner/manifest and production sources are integration-owned; no behavior corrections.\n\n## Named acceptance groups\n\nStore: absence/unavailability, stale writes, exact retry/conflicting global identity, memory atomic rollback and FileStore single-subject capability, reopen/corruption, nonadvancing observations, history/imported evidence/original receipts/complete snapshots, projections and library migration.\nExecutor: malformed and empty batches, duplicate IDs, transaction order and rollback, saved-definition recovery before load, changed retries, commit-then-uncertain and dropped response recovery, fork/merge checks, optional refusal recording versus malformed-input rejection.\n\nNative memory recorded store does not implement refusal recording or forked lineage. Supplied port fixtures may exercise real executor orchestration and must be labeled honestly; no invented native capability. Observe actual returns, histories, snapshots, receipts and provider traces. Independent authored expected values, isolated state, no boolean test wrapper. Retain a production mutation detected by a named scenario per domain, report/2 paired to exact suites, and integrate under the full repository gate.\n","status":"draft","title":"Execute storage and asynchronous executor contracts"},"entity_type":"aep.story/v1","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/er-store-executor-contracts"},"target":null,"task":null},"result":{"affected":["ent-4422067e7f12717bca8a1e5737d89bfe@1"],"audit":["aud-e9f48c90f21c15e552235c43fce7428e"],"command_id":"cmd-child-dee583d7f7fd66d9bfa866aeca654a992e948cbf703c81c7642d42622cb7d04d","consistency":"seq-000000000000","events":["evt-e9f48990f21c10cc52235b43fce740db"],"outcome":"accepted"}},"lifecycle_state":"recorded"}},"kind":"create","recording":{"actor":"human:timo","causation":"cmd-child-dee583d7f7fd66d9bfa866aeca654a992e948cbf703c81c7642d42622cb7d04d","correlation":"protocol-artifact-new","record_id":"aep.applied:child-dee583d7f7fd66d9bfa866aeca654a992e948cbf703c81c7642d42622cb7d04d@1~020d10b76e1d4c4b","recorded_at":"2026-09-28T02:07:09Z"},"subject":["aep.applied","child-dee583d7f7fd66d9bfa866aeca654a992e948cbf703c81c7642d42622cb7d04d"]}]